    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Coby Mayo** leading the offensive projections at a 65.57, largely fueled by a favorable park factor and a matchup against a pitcher with an xERA of 4.11. He is joined by **Gunnar Henderson** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** as the core of our elite-tier starts, both clearing the 63.0 threshold. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a moderate rain risk in his contest against McClanahan, the +16% park adjustment keeps him locked into our primary lineup. **Jackson Merrill** also offers significant upside; despite a slight penalty for facing a pitcher with a high stolen-base prevention rate, his 59.11 score keeps him ahead of the pack for his projected #5 spot.\n\nOur most difficult decision of the day involved **Heliot Ramos**, who finished just outside the starting rotation with a score of 45.34. While **Heliot Ramos** benefits from a slow opposing pitcher delivery that would typically boost his stolen base outlook, the optimizer favored the higher overall efficiency of **Nasim Nunez** and **Drake Baldwin**, despite their lower individual category ceilings. We are also keeping a close watch on **Liam Hicks** and **Coby Mayo** regarding the 41% rain risk at their venue; if those games are delayed or postponed, we have limited flexibility given that **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** remain unavailable on the IL. \n\nThe lineup is rounded out by the high-contact profile of **Sam Antonacci**, whose 55.30 score benefits from a positive wind forecast, and **Kyle Tucker**, who maintains a strong 58.24 despite a tougher matchup. With **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Luis Robert Jr.** providing steady baseline production, we are positioned to maximize our daily efficiency. We will continue to monitor the status of **Wade Meckler** and **Jackson Merrill** as their lineups are finalized; should their order drop significantly, we may be forced to recalibrate, though current projections suggest keeping them as our primary outfield options over the rest of the bench.",
